[#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) merged 412 reports as "dates parse mm/dd in eu locales". It is not one
bug. It is three, and only the first is what that page says.

<Callout kind="warn">
Not one issue. The queued parser fix closes problem 1 only. Problems 2 and 3 have no fix queued.
</Callout>

<SplitTable ticket={4471} />

## 1. Parser reads dates month first

The shared parser reads every date month first; day-first tenants' dates come out flipped. This
is the bug #4471 is about. Hits every day-first tenant, all channels.

## 2. booking-v3 form hint

Tenants on `booking-v3` (alder.physio, copper.studio, pale.harbour) are day-first, but the form
prints `MM/DD/YYYY` under the date field. Their people type what the hint says, month first, and
the form reads it their way: a flip the parser fix will not touch. Form channel only.

## 3. One-day move

R-41202, R-41209, R-41236, R-41344, R-41620 describe a date one day off, not a month flip
(a client in Lisbon got Tuesday, one in Toronto Monday; an invite before the booking existed).
That smells like time zones or clocks. The desk notes already single them out. Cause not yet placed.

## Why the old table hid it

<CauseTable ticket={4471} />

It counts by tenant and form only, so problem 3 sits inside `parser`, and problem 2 is marked "not
this ticket". Intake tags (`meta.intakeTag`) are a browser guess; do not triage on them.
Reports also arrive twice in the export (427 rows, 412 unique ids): count by id.

## Lessons

- Merging by subject (decision 0001) merged three causes. Check cause before merging.

